[TEXT] That confirms everything. Now I have the complete and direct evidence for the diagnosis.

**Summary of findings:**
- ICMP ping from PC1 → srv1 always worked (network path was never broken)
- TCP ports 80, 22, 443 all returned "Connection refused" — packets reached srv1 but no service was listening
- `ps aux` on srv1 showed only `named` (BIND9) running; apache2 and sshd were absent
- `/hostlab/srv1.startup` only calls `named -c /etc/bind/named.conf` — no `service apache2 start` or `service ssh start`
- Both services are installed, configured in rc2.d/rc3.d, and start correctly when invoked manually
- After manually starting both, PC1 immediately connected to port 80 and port 22 on srv1

